    "remaining_semantic_delta": "Orabona v10 printed p.2/PDF p.14 says at most sublinear and displays the ordinary inequality lim R_T(u)/T<=0 for every u. Preserve this ordinary lim display and label shared NoRegret as eventual upper-epsilon control. LimitNoRegret is the literal finite-real-limit reading. Equivalence holds only when every feasible comparator has an actual finite ordinary real limit; no unconditional equivalence or silent source replacement. Nine bridge/separation lemmas are derived reconciliation support, not nine printed theorems. For each fixed u in V and every epsilon>0, a threshold N(u,epsilon) may depend on both u and epsilon; R_T(u)/T<=epsilon for all T>=N. Separately, LimitNoRegret requires for every u in V a finite real a_u<=0 and convergence to a_u. Limits may depend on u and may be strictly negative. No uniform comparator control, absolute-value convergence, rate, nonnegative regret or zero-limit claim. One fixed infinite loss stream ell_t(x)=(F(t+1)-F(t))*x, with F(T)=T for even T and0 for odd T. Signed affine coefficients are unbounded over time. Comparator1 is feasible; it is not a squared-loss, uniformly bounded-loss, or meanPredict nonconvergence example. First four Lean-indexed losses at comparator1 are0,+2,-2,+4. CONTRACT/separate proposed repair/BODY accepted; FINAL pending. Reused distinct automated actors/history disclosed; decoder only reconstructs, no human/external/runtime attestation."
